    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0326" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg278"/>

                <head>No. 145.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Pierrepont.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 24,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, London:</hi></p>
                <p>Interview this day with Thornton makes it possible that British Government may
                    surrender Winslow, Brent, and Gray without conditions. If offer be made of all
                    or of either, you will accept, and are authorized to appoint trustworthy person
                    to convey fugitive without delay to United States.</p>
                <p>Inform me immediately by telegraph in cipher whatever be done in the
                    premises.</p>
                <closer><signed>FISH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
